Yes, true, but in D&D as far as I recall there is no particular connection 
between Shriekers and Purple Worms. A Shrieker will merely attract the 
attention of some random number of a randomly determined wandering monster.
One of the many possible monsters that _could_ be attracted is the Purple 
Worm, but it is no more likely than a Goblin or an Ogre (ignoring the fact 
that in D&D wandering monster tables, outside of wilderness adventures are 
usually tailored to produce monsters of roughly comparable threat to a 
party).

My comment concerning the connection to Dune was a speculation as to 
whether the writers had been influenced by the use of Thumpers - devices 
which send out audio signals through the desert sands - in order to attract  
the sand-worms. This relation between audio signal and attracted enormous 
worm was all I was referring to.

